From db6dc2b151ec3a7b7b15aafbadd2c703bfc4de50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 03:28:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] OCE: Report co-located 2.4/5 GHz BSSs and neighbor AP
 channels

Wi-Fi Optimized Connectivity 3.4 requires an OCE AP operating in the
2.4 or 5 GHz band to include in its Reduced Neighbor Report element at
least the BSSs it operates on other channels of these bands, and to
report the channels on which it identified neighboring APs in AP
Channel Report elements. hostapd reported only co-located 6 GHz BSSs
and had no AP Channel Report element.

For an OCE AP in these bands, report the co-located interfaces on other
2.4/5 GHz channels too, and refresh the co-located Beacon frames when
one of them starts, as for 6 GHz co-location. Report each such BSS with
the 20 MHz operating class of its primary channel, since the operating
class is to identify the primary channel together with the channel
number (IEEE Std 802.11-2024, 11.49), which a class for wider channels
does not do in these bands.

Add AP Channel Report elements, one per 20 MHz operating class, with the
channels of the APs in the neighbor report database other than the own
channel and co-located 6 GHz APs (which the Reduced Neighbor Report
element covers), and set the AP Channel Report capability in the RM
Enabled Capabilities element when there are any.

Signed-off-by: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
---
